  "slug": "mario-christian-meyer",
  "summary": "Mario-Christian Meyer is a Swiss-Brazilian physician who works to protect Amazonian biodiversity and Indigenous cultural knowledge. After studying medicine and teaching in Paris, he researched Indigenous language learning and the effects of culture on mental health. UNESCO work brought him to the Amazon, where he began advocating for cooperation between Indigenous communities and Western scientists.\n\nFrom 1992, Meyer helped develop initiatives linking traditional knowledge with biotechnology. He founded PISAD, a nonprofit focused on sustainable development, and led a UNESCO programme from 1999 to 2003. His current work seeks to transfer plant-based biotechnology to Indigenous communities, supporting local production of medicinal ingredients and economic self-reliance.\n\nMeyer received Brazil’s Giant of Ecology award in 2008 and 2017, and France named him a Knight of the Order of Merit in 2017.",
